---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Calculator from "../components/Calculator.astro";
---

<Layout>
	<Header />

	<section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pb-10 pt-12 text-center">
		<span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft px-3 py-1 font-mono text-[12px] leading-4 text-body">
			Free · No signup · Runs entirely in your browser
		</span>
		<h1 class="mt-4 font-sans text-[32px] font-semibold leading-10 tracking-[-1.28px] text-ink sm:text-[48px] sm:leading-[48px] sm:tracking-[-2.4px]">
			Know your AI API costs before you build.
		</h1>
		<p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-xl font-sans text-[18px] leading-7 text-body">
			Paste a prompt, or enter tokens or words, and compare real-time cost estimates across Claude, GPT, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Llama — with per-provider tokenization, not a flat guess.
		</p>
	</section>

	<Calculator />

	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-4 pt-24">
		<div class="space-y-10 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
			<div>
				<h2 class="font-sans text-[22px] font-semibold leading-7 tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">
					What is the AI Tokens Cost Calculator?
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
					The AI Tokens Cost Calculator is a free, browser-based tool for estimating how much a prompt or
					workload actually costs to run across today's leading language models. Instead of digging
					through seven separate pricing pages and doing the math by hand, you paste a prompt — or enter
					a token or word count — and get a side-by-side cost comparison for OpenAI, Anthropic Claude,
					Google Gemini, xAI Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral AI, and Meta Llama in seconds. As an AI model token
					cost calculator, it's built for developers, product teams, and founders who need to budget an
					API integration before writing a single line of production code.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="font-sans text-[22px] font-semibold leading-7 tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">
					How much do AI tokens cost?
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
					Every major provider bills by the token, not by the request, and input and output tokens are
					priced differently — output tokens typically cost four to six times more than input tokens on
					the same model. That makes how much tokens cost a harder question than it looks: a
					cheap-looking per-million-token rate can still add up to a large bill if your workload
					generates long responses, or if the same request runs thousands of times a day. This
					calculator handles the tokenization and the arithmetic for you, using each provider's
					published pricing per million input and output tokens, so you see a real dollar estimate
					instead of a rough guess.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="font-sans text-[22px] font-semibold leading-7 tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">
					OpenAI token price calculator
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
					Need to calculate OpenAI token price, or just get a quick OpenAI token cost calculator
					readout? Select any GPT-5.5, GPT-5.4, or GPT-5.4 nano model and the calculator tokenizes your
					prompt with OpenAI's real o200k_base tokenizer — the same encoding OpenAI's API uses
					internally — so the token count and resulting price are exact, not estimated. Use it as an
					OpenAI tokens cost calculator to line up flagship, balanced, and budget tiers side by side
					before picking a model for a new feature.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="font-sans text-[22px] font-semibold leading-7 tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">
					Anthropic Claude token cost calculator
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
					For Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Sonnet 4.6, and Claude Haiku 4.5, the tool doubles as an Anthropic
					token cost calculator and Claude token price calculator in one: enter a prompt or token count
					and get an instant estimate for each Claude tier, including how a 1M-token context window
					changes cost at scale. Anthropic doesn't publish a browser-usable tokenizer, so Claude tokens
					cost calculator results here are close algorithmic approximations rather than exact
					server-side counts — every result card flags this so you know exactly what you're looking at.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="font-sans text-[22px] font-semibold leading-7 tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">
					DeepSeek API pricing calculator
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
					DeepSeek V4-Pro and V4-Flash undercut every other flagship-class model on this page, so this
					doubles as a DeepSeek API pricing calculator for teams weighing a switch. Enter a prompt or
					token count and see DeepSeek's cost sit alongside GPT, Claude, and Gemini at the same
					workload, both with a 1M-token context window. Like the other non-OpenAI providers, DeepSeek
					doesn't publish a browser-usable tokenizer, so DeepSeek token cost calculator results here are
					close approximations rather than exact server-side counts.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="font-sans text-[22px] font-semibold leading-7 tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">
					Mistral AI token cost calculator
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
					Use this as a Mistral token price calculator across Mistral Medium 3.5, Large 3, and Small 4 —
					enter your prompt or token count once and see Mistral API pricing ranked against every other
					provider for the same input and expected output length, so you can tell whether Mistral's
					lower per-million rates actually translate into a cheaper bill for your workload.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="font-sans text-[22px] font-semibold leading-7 tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">
					Llama API cost calculator
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
					Meta doesn't run its own paid Llama API anymore, so Llama pricing here reflects Groq's hosted
					rates for Llama 3.3 70B, Llama 4 Scout, and Llama 3.1 8B — clearly labeled as "via Groq" since
					other hosts like DeepInfra, Together, and AWS Bedrock price the same open-weight models
					differently. Use it as a quick Llama token cost calculator to see where open-weight hosting
					lands relative to closed models like GPT and Claude for the same prompt.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="font-sans text-[22px] font-semibold leading-7 tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">
					Compare token cost across every AI provider
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
					Because every model runs on the same input, this also works as a way to compare token cost
					for AI providers head-to-head — Claude against GPT, Gemini against Grok, DeepSeek against
					Llama, or all seven at once — using the same prompt, the same expected output length, and
					each provider's current per-million-token pricing.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="font-sans text-[22px] font-semibold leading-7 tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">
					Find the cheapest AI model for your tokens
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
					Once you run the numbers, results are ranked automatically, so you can immediately spot the
					cheapest AI for your tokens and how much you'd save by switching tiers or providers for a
					given workload. It's a fast way to answer what's the cheapest model for my AI feature without
					building a spreadsheet — paste, compare, and decide.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="font-sans text-[22px] font-semibold leading-7 tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">
					Frequently asked questions
				</h2>
				<div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
					<div>
						<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-medium leading-6 text-ink">How much are AI tokens costing?</h3>
						<p class="mt-1 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
							AI tokens cost anywhere from about $0.05 to $5 per million input tokens depending on the
							provider and model tier, with output tokens priced four to six times higher than input
							on the same model. Budget models like Llama 3.1 8B, GPT-5.4 nano, and DeepSeek V4-Flash
							sit at the low end; flagship models like GPT-5.5, Claude Opus 4.8, and Mistral Medium
							3.5 sit at the high end. Use the calculator above for an exact price on your specific
							prompt.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-medium leading-6 text-ink">How much do 1000 tokens cost?</h3>
						<p class="mt-1 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
							Since providers price per million tokens, 1,000 tokens costs a fraction of a cent
							everywhere. Budget-tier input pricing works out to roughly $0.00005–$0.001 per 1,000
							tokens (Llama 3.1 8B, GPT-5.4 nano, DeepSeek V4-Flash), while flagship-tier input
							pricing runs about $0.002–$0.005 per 1,000 tokens (GPT-5.5, Claude Opus 4.8, Gemini 3.1
							Pro). Output tokens cost several times more per 1,000 than input tokens on every model.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-medium leading-6 text-ink">What is token cost across top AI models?</h3>
						<p class="mt-1 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
							Per million tokens (input / output), flagship pricing looks roughly like: GPT-5.5 $5 /
							$30, Claude Opus 4.8 $5 / $25, Gemini 3.1 Pro $2 / $12, Grok 4.5 $2 / $6, Mistral Medium
							3.5 $1.50 / $7.50, Llama 3.3 70B $0.59 / $0.79 (via Groq), and DeepSeek V4-Pro $0.435 /
							$0.87 — with each provider also offering cheaper balanced and budget tiers at a
							fraction of the price. Pricing changes often, so the calculator above pulls current
							per-provider rates and computes your actual cost rather than relying on a static table.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-medium leading-6 text-ink">How to compare cost of top AI models?</h3>
						<p class="mt-1 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
							Enter your workload once — paste a prompt, or set a token or word count plus expected
							output length — then select the models you want to compare, from a single provider or
							across all of them. The calculator normalizes every provider's pricing into one dollar
							total per model and ranks them cheapest to priciest, so you're comparing apples to
							apples instead of eyeballing per-token rates across seven different pricing pages.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-medium leading-6 text-ink">
							How to calculate token cost for various top AI models?
						</h3>
						<p class="mt-1 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
							The formula is the same for every provider: (input tokens ÷ 1,000,000 × input price per
							million) + (output tokens ÷ 1,000,000 × output price per million) = total cost. What
							differs is the tokenizer and the price per million tokens, which vary by model. This
							calculator automates both steps — tokenizing your prompt per model and applying each
							provider's current pricing — so you get an exact total for GPT, Claude, Gemini, Grok,
							DeepSeek, Mistral, and Llama without doing the math by hand.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-medium leading-6 text-ink">
							Does this calculator use real token counts or estimates?
						</h3>
						<p class="mt-1 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
							OpenAI counts are exact, computed with the real o200k_base tokenizer. Claude, Gemini,
							Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Llama counts are close algorithmic approximations, since
							none of those providers publish a browser-usable tokenizer — every estimate is clearly
							labeled.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-medium leading-6 text-ink">How much cheaper is DeepSeek than GPT or Claude?</h3>
						<p class="mt-1 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
							DeepSeek's flagship V4-Pro runs about 90% cheaper on input and 95%+ cheaper on output,
							per million tokens, than GPT-5.5 or Claude Opus 4.8 — and DeepSeek V4-Flash undercuts
							every budget model on this page. That gap is real, but independent evals generally
							still place GPT-5.5 and Claude Opus 4.8 ahead of DeepSeek on the hardest reasoning and
							coding tasks, so the cheapest option isn't automatically the right one for every
							workload. Run your actual prompt through the calculator above to see the dollar
							difference for your use case.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-medium leading-6 text-ink">Is my prompt uploaded anywhere?</h3>
						<p class="mt-1 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
							No. Every calculation, including tokenization, runs entirely in your browser. Nothing
							you paste is sent to a server or stored.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-medium leading-6 text-ink">How often is pricing updated?</h3>
						<p class="mt-1 font-sans text-[15px] leading-7 text-body">
							Model pricing is checked and refreshed regularly, with the last-verified date shown
							under your results. Providers change prices often, so always confirm against the
							official pricing page linked on each result card before budgeting.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "FAQPage",
		mainEntity: [
			{
