					"@type": "Answer",
					text: "AI tokens cost anywhere from about $0.05 to $5 per million input tokens depending on the provider and model tier, with output tokens priced four to six times higher than input on the same model. Budget models like Llama 3.1 8B, GPT-5.4 nano, and DeepSeek V4-Flash sit at the low end; flagship models like GPT-5.5, Claude Opus 4.8, and Mistral Medium 3.5 sit at the high end.",
				},
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				name: "How much do 1000 tokens cost?",
				acceptedAnswer: {
					"@type": "Answer",
					text: "Since providers price per million tokens, 1,000 tokens costs a fraction of a cent everywhere. Budget-tier input pricing works out to roughly $0.00005–$0.001 per 1,000 tokens (Llama 3.1 8B, GPT-5.4 nano, DeepSeek V4-Flash), while flagship-tier input pricing runs about $0.002–$0.005 per 1,000 tokens (GPT-5.5, Claude Opus 4.8, Gemini 3.1 Pro). Output tokens cost several times more per 1,000 than input tokens on every model.",
				},
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				name: "What is token cost across top AI models?",
				acceptedAnswer: {
					"@type": "Answer",
					text: "Per million tokens (input / output), flagship pricing looks roughly like: GPT-5.5 $5 / $30, Claude Opus 4.8 $5 / $25, Gemini 3.1 Pro $2 / $12, Grok 4.5 $2 / $6, Mistral Medium 3.5 $1.50 / $7.50, Llama 3.3 70B $0.59 / $0.79 (via Groq), and DeepSeek V4-Pro $0.435 / $0.87 — with each provider also offering cheaper balanced and budget tiers at a fraction of the price. Pricing changes often, so the calculator above pulls current per-provider rates and computes your actual cost rather than relying on a static table.",
				},
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				name: "How to compare cost of top AI models?",
				acceptedAnswer: {
					"@type": "Answer",
					text: "Enter your workload once — paste a prompt, or set a token or word count plus expected output length — then select the models you want to compare, from a single provider or across all of them. The calculator normalizes every provider's pricing into one dollar total per model and ranks them cheapest to priciest, so you're comparing apples to apples instead of eyeballing per-token rates across four different pricing pages.",
				},
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				name: "How to calculate token cost for various top AI models?",
				acceptedAnswer: {
					"@type": "Answer",
					text: "The formula is the same for every provider: (input tokens ÷ 1,000,000 × input price per million) + (output tokens ÷ 1,000,000 × output price per million) = total cost. What differs is the tokenizer and the price per million tokens, which vary by model. This calculator automates both steps — tokenizing your prompt per model and applying each provider's current pricing — so you get an exact total for GPT, Claude, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Llama without doing the math by hand.",
				},
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				name: "Does this calculator use real token counts or estimates?",
				acceptedAnswer: {
					"@type": "Answer",
					text: "OpenAI counts are exact, computed with the real o200k_base tokenizer. Claude, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Llama counts are close algorithmic approximations, since none of those providers publish a browser-usable tokenizer.",
				},
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				name: "How much cheaper is DeepSeek than GPT or Claude?",
				acceptedAnswer: {
					"@type": "Answer",
					text: "DeepSeek's flagship V4-Pro runs about 90% cheaper on input and 95%+ cheaper on output, per million tokens, than GPT-5.5 or Claude Opus 4.8 — and DeepSeek V4-Flash undercuts every budget model on this page. That gap is real, but independent evals generally still place GPT-5.5 and Claude Opus 4.8 ahead of DeepSeek on the hardest reasoning and coding tasks, so the cheapest option isn't automatically the right one for every workload.",
				},
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				name: "Is my prompt uploaded anywhere?",
				acceptedAnswer: {
					"@type": "Answer",
					text: "No. Every calculation, including tokenization, runs entirely in your browser. Nothing you paste is sent to a server or stored.",
				},
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				name: "How often is pricing updated?",
				acceptedAnswer: {
					"@type": "Answer",
					text: "Model pricing is checked and refreshed regularly, with the last-verified date shown under your results. Always confirm against the official pricing page before budgeting.",
				},
			},
		],
	})}
	/>

	<Footer />
</Layout>
